package com.example.disasterlink.data

/**
 * Backend base URL. This is a plain Kotlin constant instead of the AGP-
 * generated BuildConfig.API_BASE_URL field on purpose: BuildConfig is only
 * generated by actually running a Gradle build task
 * (generateDebugBuildConfig), so any editor that hasn't done that yet —
 * or a non-Android-Studio editor whose Kotlin language server doesn't
 * trigger Gradle codegen at all — shows "Unresolved reference 'BuildConfig'"
 * even though the project is otherwise fine. A plain constant in a normal
 * .kt file has no such dependency; it's always resolvable.
 *
 * MUST match your computer's LAN IP (find it with `ipconfig` on Windows or
 * `ifconfig`/`ip addr` on Mac/Linux) while the phone and backend are on the
 * same WiFi. Only use 127.0.0.1 with `adb reverse tcp:8080 tcp:8080` run
 * first, and only use 10.0.2.2 in the Android Studio emulator.
 */
object AppConfig {
    const val API_BASE_URL = "http://192.168.31.222:8080/"
}
